          },
          "message": "Publish the film, and measure the gradient-mode timings properly\n\nThe demo film is linked from the top of the README.\n\nThe per-Jacobian timings were a median of two repeats, and they moved by tens\nof percent between runs - enough to change a quoted speed-up ratio. They are\nnow a median of seven, with the per-repeat range recorded alongside so the\nspread is visible rather than implied: forward 5.84 s, batched 1.36 s, adjoint\n2.33 s. The Jacobians themselves are unchanged to every printed digit, which is\nthe part that is a property of the method rather than of the machine.\n\nAlso records the three-mode agreement in the validation record, and points at\nthe upstream compare view so the whole fork diff is one click away.",
          "tree": {
