          },
          "message": "Send all six tangent directions in one call, through a forked runtime\n\nA JVP call carried exactly one direction, because the runtime validates a\ntangent against the exact shape of its input. Six directions were therefore\nsix round trips, and each one re-assembled and re-factorised the equilibrium\noperator at every step before it ever looked at the direction. That work is\nthe whole cost of the mechanics, and it is direction-independent.\n\ntesseract-core is forked at Marc-Dvci/tesseract-core@batched-jvp to let a\ntangent carry a leading axis of k directions, with the results carrying the\nsame axis. Both images pick the fork up through the installed package, which\nis where `tesseract build` copies the runtime from.\n\nThe mechanics solver now keeps its tangent state on a leading direction axis\nand back-substitutes k times against one factorisation. The thermal side\nneeded nothing: the forked jax_jvp vmaps the batch.\n\nTwelve container derivative calls become two, and a Jacobian goes from 6.20 s\nto 1.63 s - faster than the adjoint at this design size. It agrees with\ncolumn-by-column forward mode to 8.5e-15 row by row, and the optimiser returns\nthe committed optimum bit for bit, which is the only acceptable outcome for a\nchange that is meant to cost less rather than compute differently.\n\nAlso rebuilds the feasibility-plane figure, whose legend sat on top of the\ncluster the optimiser converges into.",
